cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or the paper, please cite the work below."
title: "What Moves the Number? Evaluation and Encoder Choices Dominate Architecture in Vietnamese Spam-Review Classification"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Phan"
    given-names: "Bá Song Toàn"
  - family-names: "Trịnh"
    given-names: "Minh Bảo Trân"
  - family-names: "Trần"
    given-names: "Quang Long"
year: 2026
keywords:
  - Vietnamese NLP
  - spam review detection
  - PhoBERT
  - multi-task learning
  - reproducibility
  - evaluation
abstract: >-
  Thirty-four controlled runs on ViSpamReviews v2 measure how much each design
  choice moves macro-F1. The multi-task objective and metadata fusion move it by
  at most a tenth of a point; changing the backbone costs 1.5, and changing the
  evaluation (deduplicating training text or holding products out) moves it by
  1.4 to 2.3 points and reverses the ranking of the two models. Seed noise alone
  is 0.7 to 1.0.
